# Kimss SDK — mirror and coverage

**Source of truth:** this directory lives under private monorepo `kimssApi/kimss_sdk/`. The public `kimss-python-sdk` repo is a **git subtree force-push mirror**. Never treat the public `main` as an editable SSOT.

Cross-repo notes (local): `C:\projects\kimss-docs` → `architecture/sdk-overview.md`, `api/sdk-coverage.md`.

## Conventions

- Prefer OpenAI gateway: `base_url=https://api.kimss.ai/v1` + `X-Kimss-Agent-Id` (see AI_INTEGRATION.md).
- `client.agents.run` / `chat` / `models.create` are **deprecated** for inference.
- Public SDK param name: `conversation_id` (v2) on residual agent APIs.
- Canonical host: `https://api.kimss.ai`. Auth: `X-Kimss-Key` or Bearer on `/v1`.
- Dense HTTP map in-package: `docs/llm-context.md`.
- Platform/DB/backoffice architecture is **not** this package’s job — use kimss-docs / kimssApi `cursor_application_docs/`.

## When changing client routes

Update vault `api/sdk-coverage.md` and keep `docs/llm-context.md` in sync in the same monorepo change.
